## 5. Key Terms

| Term | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Success criterion | measurable condition used to judge product success |
| Requirement | something the client/user needs the system to do |
| Design | planned structure of the solution before development |
| Wireframe | simple sketch of a screen or page layout |
| User interface | part of the system the user interacts with |
| Input | data entered into the system |
| Output | data produced or displayed by the system |
| Data structure | way data is stored and organized |
| Database table | structured storage with fields and records |
| Algorithm | step-by-step method for solving a problem |
| Pseudocode | structured English-like way to plan an algorithm |
| Flowchart | diagram showing steps and decisions |
| Validation | checking input before it is accepted |
| Navigation | how users move between screens/pages |
| Testable | can be checked with evidence |
| Measurable | can be judged clearly rather than by opinion |
| Scope | what the project includes and excludes |
| Prototype | early model or version of the solution |
| Design decision | reasoned choice made when planning the solution |
| Evaluation link | connection between success criteria and final judgement |

