## 7. Good vs Weak Success Criteria

| Weak Success Criterion | Why Weak | Stronger Version |
|---|---|---|
| The system is useful. | too vague | The system can generate a weekly report of missing homework by student. |
| The system is easy to use. | subjective | The user can add a new record using one form with labelled fields. |
| The system looks good. | subjective | The main menu displays clearly labelled buttons for Add, Search, Report, and Exit. |
| The system is fast. | unclear measurement | Search results are displayed within two seconds for the expected dataset size. |
| The system works. | not specific | The system saves valid records and loads them again after the program restarts. |
| The system is secure. | too broad | The system does not display hidden admin options to normal users. |
| It has a database. | feature, not success | Records are stored persistently and can be retrieved after restarting the program. |

