## 11. Design Overview

Design should show how the solution will meet the criteria.

### A Strong Design May Include

```text
system overview
screen/page wireframes
navigation diagram
input/output table
data structure or database design
algorithm pseudocode
flowcharts
validation plan
test plan outline
success criteria mapping table
```

### Important

Not every project needs every diagram. Choose the design evidence that helps explain your solution clearly.

---

## 12. Success Criteria Mapping Table

A mapping table helps show that the design supports the criteria.

| Success Criterion | Design Element | Later Test Idea |
|---|---|---|
| Add homework record | Add Record form and record data structure | enter valid record and check saved |
| Search by student name | Search screen and linear search algorithm | search existing and non-existing names |
| Reject blank fields | validation rules for required fields | try saving blank name |
| Weekly summary | summary algorithm and output table | compare calculated totals with expected totals |
| Load saved records | file/database design | restart program and check data remains |

### Why Useful?

It makes the IA feel connected and planned.

