## 29. Success Criteria Checklist

Before finalizing criteria, check:

```text
Each criterion links to a client/user need.
Each criterion is specific.
Each criterion can be tested.
Each criterion can be evaluated later.
The number of criteria is manageable.
The criteria cover core features.
At least one criterion involves validation or error handling.
At least one criterion involves data storage/retrieval if relevant.
The criteria are not only about appearance.
The criteria are not too broad.
```

---

## 30. Design Checklist

Before development, check:

```text
I have planned main screens/pages.
I have planned navigation.
I have listed inputs and outputs.
I have planned data storage.
I have designed important algorithms.
I have planned validation rules.
I have linked design to success criteria.
I have included diagrams/tables where useful.
I can explain why each major design choice was made.
I have an initial testing idea for each criterion.
```

