## 31. Scenario Answer Bank

### If Asked: “What are success criteria?”

```text
Success criteria are specific and testable statements used to judge whether the final product meets the client/user needs.
```

### If Asked: “Why are success criteria important?”

```text
They guide what to build, help plan testing, and provide measurable standards for evaluation.
```

### If Asked: “What should design include?”

```text
Design should include the planned user interface, navigation, data structures, algorithms, validation, and how these meet the success criteria.
```

### If Asked: “Why is validation design important?”

```text
Validation design explains how the system will prevent or handle invalid input, and it supports later invalid data testing.
```

### If Asked: “Why use a success criteria mapping table?”

```text
It shows how each criterion is supported by the design and how it can be tested later.
```

