## 37. One-page Design and Criteria Sheet

| Area | Key Reminder |
|---|---|
| Success criteria | measurable standards for success |
| Requirement link | criteria should come from client/user needs |
| Testability | every criterion should be testable |
| Evaluation link | criteria are judged at the end |
| Good number | usually 5-8 manageable criteria |
| UI design | wireframes, layout, navigation |
| Input/output | what data enters, what output appears |
| Data design | records, tables, files, objects |
| Algorithm design | search, filter, sort, calculate, validate |
| Validation | required fields, ranges, formats |
| Mapping table | criterion → design → test |
| Design decisions | explain why choices were made |
| Common risk | vague criteria like “easy” or “good” |
| Best phrase | Success criteria define what the product must achieve, while design explains how the product will achieve it. |

